[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m2\r\u001b[26d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[mA large rock formation, worn smooth by the tide but not quite detached from the rest of the island,\r\u001b[27d"]
[0.000, "o", "marks the end of the beach. Behind it, the eastern shore of the island mostly consists of jagged\r\u001b[28d"]
[0.000, "o", "rocks and shallow tidal pools.\r\u001b[30d>"]
[2.413, "o", "n"]
[0.090, "o", "o"]
[0.091, "o", "r"]
[0.090, "o", "t"]
[0.091, "o", "h"]
[0.090, "o", "\r\u001b[2d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[8M\u001b[A\u001b[C"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7mCove            \u001b[94G"]
[0.000, "o", "3\r\u001b[23d\u001b(B\u001b[mCove\r\u001b[24d"]
[0.001, "o", "This small cove is made of a steep beach made of wet sand; the waves are a little more turbulent\r\u001b[25d"]
[0.000, "o", "here, and there seems to be movement deeper in the waters. The part of the island that rises behind\r\u001b[26d"]
[0.000, "o", "you is a steep hill covered in trees, curving up to what seems to be a plateau; this is probably not\u001b[27;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "a good approach for the climb. From here, you can follow the coast by walking in shallow waters,\r\u001b[28d"]
[0.000, "o", "towards the northwest or the south.\r\u001b[30d>"]
